<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Andernach</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Andernach is a town in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhineland-palatinate">Rhineland-Palatinate</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>, on the left bank of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhine">Rhine</a> north-west of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/koblenz">Koblenz</a>. Founded as a Roman fort, Antunnacum, it is one of the oldest towns in Germany. Two battles were fought near it in the 9th and 10th centuries, including that of 939, in which rebels against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/otto-i">Otto I</a> were defeated and Duke <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/humphrey-gilbert">Gilbert</a> of Lotharingia drowned in the Rhine.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/andernach.jpg" alt="Andernach" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Maus-Trauden at German Wikipedia · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Rheinlagen-Andernach.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
